   "id": "shabbat.89b.9",
   "daf": "89b",
   "sentenceId": 8,
   "he": "תַּבְלִין כְּדֵי לְתַבֵּל בֵּיצָה קַלָּה. וּרְמִינְהוּ: תַּבְלִין, שְׁנַיִם וּשְׁלֹשָׁה שֵׁמוֹת מִמִּין אֶחָד, אוֹ מִשְּׁלֹשָׁה מִינִין וְשֵׁם אֶחָד — אֲסוּרִין, וּמִצְטָרְפִין זֶה עִם זֶה. וְאָמַר חִזְקִיָּה:",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna that all types of «spices» join together with one another to constitute the measure «equivalent» to that which is used «to season an easily» cooked «egg. The» Gemara «raises a contradiction» from that which we learned elsewhere: «Spices,» which are prohibited due to «two or three» different «prohibitions,» e.g., one is prohibited due to orla, and one due to the prohibition of untithed produce, and they were all «of a single species» (Tosafot), «or» if they were «of three» different «species, are prohibited, and they join together with each other» to constitute a complete measure. «And Ḥizkiya said:»"
  }
 ],
